From: Artur Lorenz <lorek123@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 May 2026
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] aic_load_fw: enable BT patch loading for AIC8800D80 U02/U03

The entire BT patch-loading block in aicfw_download_fw_8800d80() is
wrapped in #if 0 in the BLUEMOON233 and goecho community drivers.  This
means fw_patch_table, fw_adid, fw_patch and fw_patch_ext0 are never
uploaded before the main firmware, so BT is silently non-functional on
any chip_id >= CHIP_REV_U02 (i.e. every real-world AIC8800D80 device).

Remove the two #if 0 / #endif guards:

  1. The outer guard that wraps the patch-table allocation and
     adid/patch address setup (chip_id detection block).

  2. The inner guard inside the FW_NORMAL_MODE / chip_id != CHIP_REV_U01
     branch that wraps the actual firmware uploads
     (fw_adid, fw_patch, ext_patch, patch_table).

The correct firmware loading order is:
  fw_patch_table_8800d80_u02.bin  (patch table)
  fw_adid_8800d80_u02.bin         (BT address ID)
  fw_patch_8800d80_u02.bin        (BT patch)
  fw_patch_8800d80_u02_ext0.bin   (BT extended patch)
  fmacfw_8800d80_u02.bin          (main WiFi+BT firmware)

The Radxa reference driver (radxa-pkg/aic8800) already has this
corrected; this patch brings the standalone community drivers into
alignment.

Fixes: BT interface (hci0) never appears on AIC8800D80 USB dongle
Tested-by: Artur Lorenz <lorek123@gmail.com>  (kernel 6.19, Bazzite 44)
---
 .../aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c  | 11 -----------
 1 file changed, 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c b/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c
index 8f5c56b..181f073 100755
